    "overview": "Preserve the incumbent Home Assistant-like administration interface: compact system typography, blue actions, neutral bordered cards and progressive disclosure. The household screen setup extends this identity rather than introducing another visual world.\n\nHome Starter owns the administrator setup and its non-operating layout preview. Generated household dashboards use native Home Assistant cards and the viewer's theme. Their chrome, typography, card styling and sidebar are Home Assistant's responsibility; do not treat those screenshot values as Home Starter tokens. V0.3 establishes admission, hierarchy and generation boundaries, not a finished visual design for every household profile. Operational limits live in [SURFACES.md](home_starter/SURFACES.md).\n\nScoped specialist world: the reference-led AirTouch overview uses navy, photographic panels, white Roboto and cyan accents. panel-* tokens apply only here; administrator styling and native control subviews retain their existing worlds. See DESIGN.md for scoped evidence and actual-hardware verification limits.",
